# `@internetdata/internetdata` is a PUBLIC package on npm, and this pins the
# scope to the registry that serves it.
#
# A no-op for anyone installing this repo normally - npmjs.org is already the
# default. It exists because a machine that also builds this brand's INTERNAL
# packages maps the whole `@internetdata` scope to a private registry, and npm
# resolves a scope to exactly one registry, so the client SDK would 404 there.
# Config is merged per key, so this overrides only the scope and leaves that
# machine's other scopes and credentials alone.
@internetdata:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
